d:'wi3',tier:'intermediate',title:'Algorithm Archipelago',subtitle:'The classic ML toolbox',emoji:'\ud83c\udfdd\ufe0f',lessons:[{id:'wi3l1',title:'Regression',emoji:'\ud83d\udcc8',xp:80,cards:[{emoji:'\ud83d\udcc8',title:'Linear regression',body:'The "hello world" of ML: fit a straight line through data points to predict numbers (house prices, temperatures). Simple, fast, and surprisingly powerful.'},{emoji:'\ud83c\udf9a\ufe0f',title:'Logistic regression',body:'Despite the name, it\'s for CLASSIFICATION \u2014 it squashes outputs into probabilities (0 to 1) to answer yes/no questions like "spam or not?".'},{emoji:'\ud83e\uddee',title:'When to use them',body:'Small data? Need explainability? Regressions are still industry workhorses. Not everything needs deep learning \u2014 cert exams test this judgment!'}],quiz:[{question:'Logistic regression is used for\u2026',options:['Predicting numbers','Classification','Clustering','Image generation'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'It outputs probabilities for classes \u2014 a classification tool.'},{question:'Predicting a house price is a ______ problem.',options:['Classification','Clustering','Regression','Generation'],answerIndex:2,explanation:'Predicting continuous numbers = regression.'}]},{id:'wi3l2',title:'Trees & Ensembles',emoji:'\ud83c\udf33',xp:80,cards:[{emoji:'\ud83c\udf33',title:'Decision trees',body:'A flowchart of yes/no questions: "Income > 50k? Age > 30?" Easy to understand, easy to overfit. Humans love them because you can literally read the logic.'},{emoji:'\ud83c\udf32',title:'Random forests',body:'Train many trees on random slices of data, let them vote. The crowd of weak trees becomes a strong, stable predictor. Ensemble magic!'},{emoji:'\ud83d\ude80',title:'Gradient boosting',body:'XGBoost & friends build trees one at a time, each fixing the previous one\'s mistakes. Still wins most tabular-data competitions \u2014 beating neural nets!'}],quiz:[{question:'A random forest is\u2026',options:['One deep tree','Many trees voting together','A neural network','A database'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'Ensembles of trees reduce overfitting via voting.'},{question:'For tabular business data, a top performer is often\u2026',options:['Gradient boosting (XGBoost)','CNNs','Diffusion models','RNNs'],answerIndex:0,explanation:'Boosted trees still dominate structured/tabular data.'}]},{id:'wi3l3',title:'Clustering & KNN',emoji:'\ud83e\udee7',xp:80,cards:[{emoji:'\ud83e\udee7',title:'K-means clustering',body:'Pick K group centers, assign each point to its nearest center, move centers to the average, repeat. Boom \u2014 customer segments, without any labels.'},{emoji:'\ud83c\udfd8\ufe0f',title:'K-nearest neighbors',body:'To classify a new point, just look at its K closest neighbors and copy the majority vote. No training phase at all \u2014 the data IS the model.'},{emoji:'\ud83d\udccf',title:'Distance is everything',body:'Both methods rely on measuring distance between points \u2014 which is why feature scaling (normalizing ranges) matters so much.'}],quiz:[{question:'K-means is a ______ algorithm.',options:['Supervised','Clustering (unsupervised)','Reinforcement','Generative'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'It groups unlabeled data into K clusters.'},{question:'KNN classifies a point by\u2026',options:['Deep layers','Its nearest neighbors\' votes','Random guessing','Gradient descent'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'Majority vote of the K closest points.'}]},{id:'wi3l4',title:'Judging Models',emoji:'\u2696\ufe0f',xp:90,cards:[{emoji:'\ud83c\udfaf',title:'Accuracy can lie',body:'A disease affects 1% of people. A model saying "healthy" to everyone scores 99% accuracy \u2014 and is useless! That\'s why we need better metrics.'},{emoji:'\ud83d\udd0d',title:'Precision vs Recall',body:'Precision: of the ones I flagged, how many were right? Recall: of all the real cases, how many did I catch? Spam filters want precision; cancer screening wants recall.'},{emoji:'\ud83d\udcca',title:'Confusion matrix & F1',body:'The confusion matrix shows true/false positives/negatives. F1 combines precision & recall into one number. Cert exams LOVE these questions.'}],quiz:[{question:'Catching every real cancer case matters most \u2014 optimize\u2026',options:['Accuracy','Recall','Speed','Model size'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'Recall measures how many true cases you catch \u2014 missing one is costly.'},{question:'Why is accuracy misleading on imbalanced data?',options:['It\'s too slow','Majority-class guessing scores high','It needs GPUs','It isn\'t'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'Always predicting the common class gives high accuracy but zero value.'},{question:'F1 score combines\u2026',options:['Speed & size','Precision & recall','Loss & accuracy','Bias & variance'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'F1 is the harmonic mean of precision and recall.'}]}]},{id:'wi4',tier:'intermediate',title:'Sequence Springs',subtitle:'AI for things that flow',emoji:'\ud83c\udf0a',lessons:[{id:'wi4l1',title:'RNNs & Memory',emoji:'\ud83d\udd01',xp:90,cards:[{emoji:'\ud83d\udd01',title:'Recurrent networks',body:'RNNs process sequences step by step, carrying a hidden "memory" forward \u2014 perfect for text, audio, and time series where order matters.'},{emoji:'\ud83e\udde0',title:'LSTM: better memory',body:'Plain RNNs forget quickly (vanishing gradients). LSTMs add gates that control what to remember and forget \u2014 dominating NLP until Transformers arrived.'},{emoji:'\u26a1',title:'Why Transformers won',body:'RNNs read one word at a time; Transformers read everything at once with attention \u2014 massively parallel, faster to train, better at long-range context.'}],quiz:[{question:'RNNs are designed for\u2026',options:['Static images','Sequential data','Databases','Spreadsheets'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'Their memory loop makes them fit text, audio, and time series.'},{question:'Transformers beat RNNs partly because they\u2026',options:['Process tokens in parallel','Are smaller','Use no math','Run on CPUs only'],answerIndex:0,explanation:'Attention processes whole sequences at once \u2014 huge speed and context wins.'}]},{id:'wi4l2',title:'Time Series & Forecasting',emoji:'\ud83d\udcc9',xp:90,cards:[{emoji:'\ud83d\udcc9',title:'Predicting the future',body:'Sales, weather, stock demand, server load \u2014 time series forecasting predicts future values from past patterns: trend, seasonality, and noise.'},{emoji:'\ud83d\uddd3\ufe0f',title:'Seasonality',body:'Ice cream sales spike each summer; website traffic dips each weekend. Good models learn these repeating cycles, not just the overall trend.'},{emoji:'\u2601\ufe0f',title:'In the cloud',body:'AWS Forecast, Azure ML AutoML, and Vertex AI forecasting offer managed time-series prediction \u2014 a common cert exam scenario for demand planning.'}],quiz:[{question:'Repeating yearly/weekly patterns in data are called\u2026',options:['Noise','Seasonality','Drift','Bias'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'Seasonality = regular repeating cycles.'},{question:'Forecasting next month\'s sales is a ______ problem.',options:['Classification','Time series regression','Clustering','Image'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'Predicting future continuous values from historical sequence data.'}]}]},{id:'wa3',tier:'advanced',title:'Frontier Frontier',subtitle:'Where AI is heading',emoji:'\ud83d\udef8',lessons:[{id:'wa3l1',title:'Fine-tuning & LoRA',emoji:'\ud83c\udf9b\ufe0f',xp:130,cards:[{emoji:'\ud83c\udf9b\ufe0f',title:'Customizing LLMs',body:'Options from cheap to expensive: prompt engineering \u2192 RAG \u2192 fine-tuning \u2192 training from scratch. Always try the cheaper option first \u2014 a classic cert exam answer!'},{emoji:'\ud83e\udeb6',title:'LoRA: light fine-tuning',body:'Instead of updating billions of weights, LoRA trains tiny "adapter" matrices \u2014 1000x fewer parameters, nearly the same quality. Fine-tuning on a single GPU became possible.'},{emoji:'\ud83e\uddea',title:'When to fine-tune',body:'Fine-tune for style, format, or domain language. Use RAG for facts and fresh knowledge. Mixing them up is the #1 architecture mistake (and favorite exam trap).'}],quiz:[{question:'Cheapest first step to improve LLM outputs?',options:['Train from scratch','Prompt engineering','Buy GPUs','Fine-tune'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'Always start with prompting \u2014 zero training cost.'},{question:'For up-to-date factual answers, prefer\u2026',options:['RAG','Fine-tuning','Bigger batch size','More layers'],answerIndex:0,explanation:'RAG retrieves current facts; fine-tuning bakes in style, not fresh knowledge.'}]},{id:'wa3l2',title:'Multimodal AI',emoji:'\ud83c\udf08',xp:130,cards:[{emoji:'\ud83c\udf08',title:'Beyond text',body:'Multimodal models handle text + images + audio + video in one brain. Describe a photo, generate an image from words, watch a video and summarize it.'},{emoji:'\ud83d\udd17',title:'Shared embedding space',body:'The trick: map every modality into the same vector space, so "a photo of a dog" and the word "dog" land close together. CLIP pioneered this.'},{emoji:'\ud83e\udd16',title:'Embodied AI',body:'The frontier: multimodal models controlling robots \u2014 seeing, planning, and acting in the physical world. Vision + language + action models are the hottest research area.'}],quiz:[{question:'Multimodal models process\u2026',options:['Only text','Multiple data types (text, image, audio\u2026)','Only numbers','Only code'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'One model, many modalities.'},{question:'CLIP aligns images and text by\u2026',options:['Mapping both into a shared embedding space','Copying pixels','Using keywords','Random matching'],answerIndex:0,explanation:'Shared vector space = cross-modal understanding.'}]},{id:'wa3l3',title:'AI Safety & Alignment',emoji:'\ud83d\udee1\ufe0f',xp:140,cards:[{emoji:'\ud83c\udfaf',title:'The alignment problem',body:'How do we ensure powerful AI does what we MEAN, not just what we SAY? An AI told to "maximize clicks" might learn to spread outrage. Specifying goals safely is deceptively hard.'},{emoji:'\ud83e\uddd1\u200d\u2696\ufe0f',title:'RLHF',body:'Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback: humans rank model outputs, a reward model learns those preferences, and the LLM is tuned toward them. It\'s why chatbots are helpful instead of chaotic.'},{emoji:'\ud83d\udea8',title:'Real risks today',body:'Hallucinations, prompt injection, jailbreaks, deepfakes, and bias. Every cloud provider now ships guardrails (content filters, grounding checks) \u2014 know them for cert exams.'}],quiz:[{question:'RLHF tunes models using\u2026',options:['More internet text','Human preference rankings','Random rewards','Bigger GPUs'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'Humans rank outputs; the model learns to match those preferences.'},{question:'Tricking an LLM via malicious input text is called\u2026',options:['Prompt injection','Data drift','Overfitting','Pooling'],answerIndex:0,explanation:'Prompt injection hides adversarial instructions in the input.'}]}]},{id:'wa4',tier:'advanced',title:'Cert Bootcamp',subtitle:'Exam-style practice, all clouds',emoji:'\ud83c\udf96\ufe0f',lessons:[{id:'wa4l1',title:'AWS AI Drill',emoji:'\ud83d\udfe7',xp:150,cards:[{emoji:'\ud83d\udfe7',title:'AWS AI service map',body:'SageMaker (build/train/deploy ML), Bedrock (managed LLMs/GenAI), Rekognition (vision), Comprehend (NLP), Transcribe (speech\u2192text), Polly (text\u2192speech), Lex (chatbots), Textract (documents).'},{emoji:'\ud83e\udded',title:'Exam mindset',body:'AWS exams test service SELECTION: "least operational overhead" usually means the managed AI service, not building your own model on SageMaker.'},{emoji:'\ud83d\udcdc',title:'AI Practitioner focus',body:'Know GenAI basics, Bedrock features (agents, guardrails, knowledge bases), responsible AI tools, and when to prompt vs RAG vs fine-tune.'}],quiz:[{question:'Extract text and tables from scanned invoices on AWS:',options:['Textract','Polly','Lex','Rekognition'],answerIndex:0,explanation:'Textract is AWS\'s document text/table extraction service.'},{question:'Managed access to foundation models on AWS is\u2026',options:['Bedrock','EC2','S3','Lambda'],answerIndex:0,explanation:'Bedrock = serverless foundation models with guardrails and agents.'},{question:'"Least operational overhead" for sentiment analysis:',options:['Comprehend','Custom model on EC2','Build from scratch','A spreadsheet'],answerIndex:0,explanation:'Managed service beats custom builds when requirements are standard.'}]},{id:'wa4l2',title:'Azure AI Drill',emoji:'\ud83d\udfe6',xp:150,cards:[{emoji:'\ud83d\udfe6',title:'Azure AI service map',body:'Azure Machine Learning (ML platform), Azure OpenAI (GPT models), AI Vision, AI Language, AI Speech, AI Document Intelligence, AI Search (vector/RAG), Bot Service.'},{emoji:'\ud83c\udf93',title:'AI-901 & AI-500',body:'AI-901 covers AI concepts, Microsoft Foundry services, and responsible AI. AI-500 moves into engineering multi-agent solutions with orchestration, tools, knowledge, observability, and security.'},{emoji:'\ud83d\udee1\ufe0f',title:'Microsoft\'s 6 principles',body:'Fairness, Reliability & Safety, Privacy & Security, Inclusiveness, Transparency, and Accountability remain core responsible-AI concepts for AI-901 and production systems.'}],quiz:[{question:'Azure\'s service for RAG-style vector search is\u2026',options:['AI Search','Blob Storage','Cosmos DB only','Azure Functions'],answerIndex:0,explanation:'Azure AI Search provides vector + hybrid retrieval for RAG.'},{question:'Which is one of Microsoft\'s responsible AI principles?',options:['Profitability','Transparency','Speed','Scale'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'The six principles include Transparency and Accountability.'},{question:'GPT-4 class models on Azure come via\u2026',options:['Azure OpenAI','Azure DevOps','Azure VM only','Excel'],answerIndex:0,explanation:'Azure OpenAI Service hosts OpenAI models with enterprise controls.'}]},{id:'wa4l3',title:'GCP AI Drill',emoji:'\ud83d\udfe9',xp:150,cards:[{emoji:'\ud83d\udfe9',title:'Google Cloud AI map',body:'Vertex AI (unified ML platform + Gemini models), AutoML (no-code training), Vision AI, Natural Language AI, Speech-to-Text, Translation, Document AI, BigQuery ML (SQL-based ML).'},{emoji:'\ud83d\udd2e',title:'BigQuery ML superpower',body:'Train models with plain SQL right where your data lives \u2014 no data movement. Exam favorite: analysts who know SQL but not Python \u2192 BigQuery ML.'},{emoji:'\ud83c\udfd7\ufe0f',title:'ML Engineer exam',body:'Tests the full lifecycle: data pipelines, training at scale, deployment (endpoints vs batch), monitoring, and MLOps with Vertex AI Pipelines.'}],quiz:[{question:'SQL analysts training models without Python should use\u2026',options:['BigQuery ML','Raw TensorFlow','Kubernetes','Sheets'],answerIndex:0,explanation:'BigQuery ML trains models using SQL directly in the warehouse.'},{question:'Google\'s unified ML platform is\u2026',options:['Vertex AI','SageMaker','Azure ML','Colab'],answerIndex:0,explanation:'Vertex AI = training, deployment, pipelines, and Gemini access.'},{question:'For serving real-time predictions, use\u2026',options:['An online endpoint','Batch prediction','A CSV export','Email'],answerIndex:0,explanation:'Online endpoints serve low-latency real-time requests; batch is for bulk offline jobs.'}]}]}]},280,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"certWorlds",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}});const t=[{id:'ce1',tier:'beginner',title:'Vision & Language Bay',subtitle:'Azure AI-901 workloads',emoji:'\ud83c\udf09',lessons:[{id:'ce1l1',title:'Computer Vision Workloads',emoji:'\ud83d\udcf7',xp:70,cards:[{emoji:'\ud83c\udff7\ufe0f',title:'Classification vs detection',body:'Image classification answers "WHAT is this picture?" (one label). Object detection answers "WHAT is WHERE?" (boxes around each object). Semantic segmentation labels every pixel. Know the difference \u2014 AI-901 expects you to distinguish them!'},{emoji:'\ud83d\udd24',title:'OCR & document AI',body:'Optical Character Recognition extracts text from images: receipts, signs, handwriting. Document intelligence goes further \u2014 understanding forms, tables, and invoices (Azure Document Intelligence, AWS Textract, Google Document AI).'},{emoji:'\ud83d\ude42',title:'Face & video analysis',body:'Face detection finds faces; face recognition identifies WHO (heavily regulated!). Video analysis adds tracking, transcript generation, and scene detection. Azure AI Vision, Rekognition, and Cloud Vision cover these.'}],quiz:[{question:'Drawing boxes around each car in a photo is\u2026',options:['Classification','Object detection','OCR','Clustering'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'Detection = locating and labeling multiple objects with boxes.'},{question:'Extracting text from a scanned receipt uses\u2026',options:['OCR','Face detection','Regression','Clustering'],answerIndex:0,explanation:'Optical Character Recognition reads text from images.'}]},{id:'ce1l2',title:'NLP Workloads',emoji:'\ud83d\udcac',xp:70,cards:[{emoji:'\ud83d\ude0a',title:'Sentiment & key phrases',body:'Sentiment analysis scores text positive/negative/neutral \u2014 perfect for reviews and support tickets. Key phrase extraction pulls the main topics. Azure AI Language, AWS Comprehend, and Cloud Natural Language do both.'},{emoji:'\ud83c\udff7\ufe0f',title:'Entity recognition',body:'Named Entity Recognition (NER) finds people, places, dates, and organizations in text: "Satya visited Paris in May" \u2192 person, location, date. PII detection is a special version that finds sensitive data to mask.'},{emoji:'\ud83c\udf10',title:'Translation & speech',body:'Neural translation preserves meaning across 100+ languages. Speech services: speech-to-text (transcription), text-to-speech (natural voices), speech translation (both at once!). Azure AI Speech is a key AI-901 service family.'}],quiz:[{question:'Scoring reviews as positive/negative is\u2026',options:['Sentiment analysis','OCR','Clustering','Detection'],answerIndex:0,explanation:'Sentiment analysis classifies emotional tone.'},{question:'Finding "Paris" as a location in text is\u2026',options:['Translation','Entity recognition (NER)','Summarization','TTS'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'NER identifies and types named entities.'}]},{id:'ce1l3',title:'Conversational AI',emoji:'\ud83e\udd16',xp:80,cards:[{emoji:'\ud83c\udfaf',title:'Intents & utterances',body:'An utterance is what the user says ("book me a flight"). The intent is what they want (BookFlight). Entities fill the details (destination, date). Classic bots map utterances \u2192 intents \u2192 actions.'},{emoji:'\ud83d\udcac',title:'Dialog management',body:'Multi-turn conversations need state: what was asked, what\'s still missing ("Which city?" \u2192 "What date?"). Dialog systems track context across turns \u2014 Azure Bot Service + Bot Framework handle the plumbing.'},{emoji:'\ud83e\udde0',title:'LLM-era bots',body:'Modern bots use LLMs (Azure OpenAI, Bedrock, Gemini) with grounding on company data, safety filters, and tool calling \u2014 replacing rigid intent trees with flexible natural conversation. AI-901 covers generative-AI workloads alongside traditional conversational AI.'}],quiz:[{question:'"Book me a flight to Tokyo" \u2014 BookFlight is the\u2026',options:['Utterance','Intent','Entity','Dialog'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'Intent = the user\'s goal; the sentence is the utterance; Tokyo is an entity.'},{question:'Multi-turn bots must track\u2026',options:['GPU usage','Conversation state/context','IP addresses','Nothing'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'Dialog management carries context across turns.'}]}]},{id:'ce2',tier:'intermediate',title:'Data Engineering Docks',subtitle:'Fuel pipelines for ML',emoji:'\u2693',lessons:[{id:'ce2l1',title:'Ingestion & ETL',emoji:'\ud83d\ude9a',xp:90,cards:[{emoji:'\ud83d\ude9a',title:'ETL vs ELT',body:'ETL: Extract \u2192 Transform \u2192 Load (clean before storing). ELT: load raw into a warehouse, transform there with SQL power. Modern clouds favor ELT \u2014 storage is cheap, warehouses are mighty.'},{emoji:'\ud83c\udf0a',title:'Batch vs streaming',body:'Batch: process chunks on a schedule (nightly sales reports). Streaming: process events as they arrive (fraud alerts in milliseconds). Streaming tools: Kinesis (AWS), Event Hubs (Azure), Pub/Sub + Dataflow (GCP).'},{emoji:'\ud83d\uddc4\ufe0f',title:'The AWS data lineup',body:'S3 (data lake storage), Glue (serverless ETL + catalog), Athena (SQL directly on S3), Redshift (warehouse), and Kinesis (streams). Current AWS ML Engineer scenarios test which managed data service fits each workload.'}],quiz:[{question:'Real-time fraud detection needs\u2026',options:['Batch processing','Streaming ingestion','Monthly reports','Manual review'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'Millisecond decisions require streaming (e.g. Kinesis).'},{question:'Serverless SQL queries directly on S3 files use\u2026',options:['Athena','EC2','SageMaker','Lambda'],answerIndex:0,explanation:'Athena queries S3 data lakes with plain SQL.'}]},{id:'ce2l2',title:'Data Prep Mastery',emoji:'\ud83e\uddfc',xp:90,cards:[{emoji:'\ud83d\udd73\ufe0f',title:'Missing values & outliers',body:'Missing data: drop rows, impute with mean/median, or flag with an indicator. Outliers: investigate first (fraud? typo?), then cap, transform, or remove. Wrong handling silently poisons models.'},{emoji:'\u2696\ufe0f',title:'Class imbalance',body:'99% legit / 1% fraud breaks naive training. Fixes: oversample the minority (SMOTE), undersample the majority, class weights, or better metrics (precision/recall, not accuracy!).'},{emoji:'\ud83c\udff7\ufe0f',title:'Labeling at scale',body:'Ground truth comes from humans: SageMaker Ground Truth, Azure ML labeling, Vertex labeling jobs. Pro tricks: active learning (label the most informative samples first) and consensus voting for quality.'}],quiz:[{question:'SMOTE is used for\u2026',options:['Faster GPUs','Oversampling minority classes','Data encryption','Deployment'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'It synthesizes minority-class examples to balance training.'},{question:'Best first response to outliers is\u2026',options:['Always delete them','Investigate their cause','Ignore them','Double them'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'Outliers may be errors \u2014 or your most important signal (fraud!).'}]},{id:'ce2l3',title:'EDA & Feature Insights',emoji:'\ud83d\udd2c',xp:100,cards:[{emoji:'\ud83d\udcca',title:'Profiling & distributions',body:'Before modeling, profile everything: ranges, uniques, nulls, distributions (normal? skewed?). Skewed features often need log transforms. Correlation heatmaps reveal redundant features.'},{emoji:'\ud83d\udcc9',title:'Dimensionality reduction',body:'PCA compresses hundreds of correlated features into a few "principal components" retaining most variance. t-SNE/UMAP visualize clusters in 2D. Fewer dimensions = faster, less overfitting-prone models.'},{emoji:'\ud83e\uddea',title:'Experiment tracking',body:'Every run logs params, data version, metrics: MLflow, SageMaker Experiments, Vertex Experiments, Azure ML jobs. Reproducibility = "which exact combo produced our best model?" answered in seconds.'}],quiz:[{question:'PCA is used for\u2026',options:['Labeling','Dimensionality reduction','Deployment','Streaming'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'Principal Component Analysis compresses features while keeping variance.'},{question:'Experiment tracking records\u2026',options:['Params, data versions & metrics per run','Only final models','User emails','GPU temps'],answerIndex:0,explanation:'Full lineage makes results reproducible and comparable.'}]}]},{id:'ce3',tier:'intermediate',title:'Metrics Lab',subtitle:'Judge models like a pro',emoji:'\ud83e\uddea',lessons:[{id:'ce3l1',title:'Advanced Metrics',emoji:'\ud83d\udccf',xp:90,cards:[{emoji:'\ud83d\udcc8',title:'ROC-AUC',body:'The ROC curve plots true-positive rate vs false-positive rate across all thresholds. AUC (area under it): 1.0 = perfect ranking, 0.5 = coin flip. Great for comparing classifiers independent of threshold choice.'},{emoji:'\ud83d\udcd0',title:'RMSE vs MAE',body:'Regression errors: MAE = average absolute miss (robust, interpretable). RMSE squares errors first \u2014 punishing BIG misses hard. Predicting house prices where huge errors are costly? Watch RMSE.'},{emoji:'\ud83d\udd0d',title:'Error analysis',body:'Don\'t just read one number \u2014 slice errors by segment: does the model fail on new users? Night images? A specific region? Fixing the worst slice beats tuning global metrics. Pros live in the confusion matrix.'}],quiz:[{question:'AUC of 0.5 means the classifier is\u2026',options:['Perfect','As good as random','Overfit','Fast'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'0.5 = no ranking ability \u2014 a coin flip.'},{question:'RMSE differs from MAE by\u2026',options:['Punishing large errors more','Being always smaller','Ignoring errors','Working only for images'],answerIndex:0,explanation:'Squaring amplifies big misses before averaging.'}]},{id:'ce3l2',title:'Learning Types & Sampling',emoji:'\ud83c\udf9b\ufe0f',xp:90,cards:[{emoji:'\ud83c\udf17',title:'Semi & self-supervised',body:'Semi-supervised: few labels + lots of unlabeled data (label a little, propagate). Self-supervised: the data labels itself \u2014 predict the next token, fill masked words. It\'s how LLMs pretrain without human labels!'},{emoji:'\ud83c\udfb2',title:'Top-k & top-p sampling',body:'Top-k: sample from only the k most likely next tokens. Top-p (nucleus): sample from the smallest set covering p% probability \u2014 adapts to confidence. Combine with temperature to dial creativity precisely.'},{emoji:'\ud83d\udd27',title:'Prompt tuning vs fine-tuning',body:'Prompt tuning trains tiny "soft prompt" vectors while freezing the model \u2014 cheaper than fine-tuning, more robust than manual prompts. The middle rung of the customization ladder (AWS AIF tests this!).'}],quiz:[{question:'LLM pretraining (predict next token) is\u2026',options:['Supervised by humans','Self-supervised','Reinforcement','Unlabeled clustering'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'The data provides its own labels \u2014 the next token.'},{question:'Top-p sampling picks from\u2026',options:['All tokens equally','The smallest set covering p probability','Only 1 token','Random tokens'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'Nucleus sampling adapts the candidate pool to model confidence.'}]}]},{id:'ce4',tier:'advanced',title:'Security Citadel',subtitle:'Protect & govern AI',emoji:'\ud83d\udd10',lessons:[{id:'ce4l1',title:'AI Security Foundations',emoji:'\ud83d\udee1\ufe0f',xp:130,cards:[{emoji:'\ud83d\udd11',title:'IAM for AI',body:'Identity & Access Management controls WHO can call models, access training data, or deploy. Principle of least privilege: grant the minimum needed. Every AWS AI Practitioner exam has IAM questions!'},{emoji:'\ud83d\udd12',title:'Encryption everywhere',body:'At rest: data encrypted in S3/storage (KMS keys). In transit: TLS on every API call. Customer-managed keys (CMK) when regulations demand you control the keys. Models and embeddings need encryption too!'},{emoji:'\ud83d\udcdc',title:'Auditability',body:'CloudTrail (AWS), Azure Monitor, Cloud Audit Logs: record every model invocation, data access, and config change. When someone asks "who queried the customer model last Tuesday?", logs answer instantly.'}],quiz:[{question:'Least privilege means\u2026',options:['No one gets access','Grant only the minimum needed permissions','Everyone is admin','Passwords only'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'Minimal permissions shrink the blast radius of any compromise.'},{question:'Data encrypted "at rest" protects it\u2026',options:['During API calls','While stored on disk','During training only','Never'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'At rest = in storage; in transit = moving over networks.'}]},{id:'ce4l2',title:'Governance & Compliance',emoji:'\u2696\ufe0f',xp:140,cards:[{emoji:'\ud83c\udf0d',title:'Data residency & privacy',body:'Some data legally cannot leave its country/region (GDPR, healthcare laws). Choose regions carefully, know what the provider does with your prompts (training on them? retention?), and mask PII before it reaches models.'},{emoji:'\ud83c\udfdb\ufe0f',title:'AI governance programs',body:'Model inventories, risk classification (EU AI Act tiers), approval workflows, usage policies, and periodic reviews. Governance turns "responsible AI" from slideware into enforced practice.'},{emoji:'\ud83d\udea7',title:'Guardrails as policy',body:'Bedrock Guardrails, Azure Content Safety, and Vertex safety filters enforce org-wide rules: blocked topics, PII masking, grounding checks. Centralized guardrails > per-app prompt patching.'}],quiz:[{question:'Data residency requirements dictate\u2026',options:['Model size','Where data may be stored/processed geographically','GPU brand','Token limits'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'Laws like GDPR restrict data to specific regions.'},{question:'A model inventory is part of\u2026',options:['AI governance','GPU cooling','Prompt design','Tokenization'],answerIndex:0,explanation:'Governance tracks what models exist, their risk, and their approval status.'}]}]}]},281,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"skillWorlds",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return t}});const t=[{id:'sk1',tier:'beginner',title:'Python Peninsula',subtitle:'The language of AI',emoji:'\ud83d\udc0d',lessons:[{id:'sk1l1',title:'Why Python Runs AI',emoji:'\ud83d\udc0d',xp:60,cards:[{emoji:'\ud83d\udc0d',title:'The lingua franca',body:'Python won AI because it reads like English and glues to fast C/GPU code underneath. Every major framework \u2014 PyTorch, TensorFlow, scikit-learn, Hugging Face \u2014 speaks Python first.'},{emoji:'\ud83d\udce6',title:'The core toolkit',body:'NumPy (fast arrays & math), pandas (tables/DataFrames), matplotlib (plots), scikit-learn (classic ML), PyTorch (deep learning), Hugging Face (pretrained models). Six libraries = 95% of daily AI work.'},{emoji:'\ud83d\udcd3',title:'Notebooks',body:'Jupyter notebooks mix code, results, and notes in one document \u2014 the standard for experiments. Google Colab gives you free GPU notebooks in the browser: zero setup deep learning!'}],quiz:[{question:'The standard library for DataFrame tables is\u2026',options:['NumPy','pandas','matplotlib','PyTorch'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'pandas = tabular data manipulation and analysis.'},{question:'Free browser GPUs for notebooks come from\u2026',options:['Google Colab','Excel','Notepad','Slack'],answerIndex:0,explanation:'Colab runs Jupyter notebooks with free GPU access.'}]},{id:'sk1l2',title:'Reading AI Code',emoji:'\ud83d\udc53',xp:70,cards:[{emoji:'\ud83d\udd22',title:'Tensors & shapes',body:'Everything is a tensor (n-dimensional array). A batch of 32 RGB images of 224\xd7224 = shape [32, 3, 224, 224]. Reading shapes is THE core skill \u2014 90% of deep learning bugs are shape mismatches!'},{emoji:'\ud83d\udd01',title:'The training loop',body:'Every PyTorch project: for each batch \u2192 forward pass (predict) \u2192 compute loss \u2192 backward pass (gradients) \u2192 optimizer step (update weights) \u2192 repeat. Recognize this loop and you can read any repo.'},{emoji:'\ud83e\udd17',title:'The 5-line revolution',body:'from transformers import pipeline; pipe = pipeline("sentiment-analysis"); pipe("I love this!"). Hugging Face made state-of-the-art AI a 3-liner. Standing on giants\' shoulders is the professional way.'}],quiz:[{question:'Most deep learning bugs come from\u2026',options:['Tensor shape mismatches','Slow internet','Wrong fonts','Small screens'],answerIndex:0,explanation:'Shape errors are the #1 debugging task \u2014 always print shapes!'},{question:'The PyTorch training loop order is\u2026',options:['Forward \u2192 loss \u2192 backward \u2192 step','Step \u2192 loss \u2192 forward','Backward \u2192 forward','Random'],answerIndex:0,explanation:'Predict, measure error, compute gradients, update weights.'}]}]},{id:'sk2',tier:'beginner',title:'Math Mountain',subtitle:'Just enough math to be dangerous',emoji:'\u26f0\ufe0f',lessons:[{id:'sk2l1',title:'Statistics Survival Kit',emoji:'\ud83d\udcca',xp:70,cards:[{emoji:'\ud83d\udcca',title:'Mean, median, spread',body:'Mean = average (sensitive to outliers). Median = middle value (robust \u2014 use for incomes!). Standard deviation = typical distance from the mean. These three describe any dataset in seconds.'},{emoji:'\ud83d\udd14',title:'Distributions',body:'The normal (bell) curve appears everywhere: heights, errors, noise. 68% within 1 std dev, 95% within 2. Skewed distributions (income, city sizes) need medians and log transforms.'},{emoji:'\ud83c\udfaf',title:'Correlation \u2260 causation',body:'Ice cream sales correlate with drownings (both rise in summer!). Correlation finds patterns; only experiments (A/B tests) prove causation. The most important sentence in data science.'}],quiz:[{question:'For skewed data like incomes, prefer the\u2026',options:['Mean','Median','Mode','Max'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'The median resists outlier billionaires.'},{question:'Ice cream sales and drownings correlate because\u2026',options:['Ice cream causes drowning','A shared cause: summer','Coincidence only','Bad data'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'A confounder (season) drives both \u2014 correlation \u2260 causation.'}]},{id:'sk2l2',title:'Probability for AI',emoji:'\ud83c\udfb2',xp:70,cards:[{emoji:'\ud83c\udfb2',title:'Conditional probability',body:'P(A|B) = probability of A given B happened. Spam filtering is P(spam | contains "free money"). Almost every classifier outputs conditional probabilities.'},{emoji:'\ud83e\uddee',title:'Bayes\' theorem',body:'Update beliefs with evidence: P(disease|positive test) depends on the base rate! A 99%-accurate test on a rare disease still yields mostly false positives. This trips up doctors \u2014 and exam takers.'},{emoji:'\ud83d\udcc9',title:'Expected value',body:'Average outcome weighted by probability. AI decisions maximize expected value: recommend the movie with the highest expected rating, take the action with the highest expected reward (that\'s reinforcement learning!).'}],quiz:[{question:'A 99% accurate test for a 1-in-10,000 disease mostly gives\u2026',options:['True positives','False positives','Perfect results','No results'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'Base rates dominate \u2014 Bayes\' theorem in action.'},{question:'Reinforcement learning maximizes\u2026',options:['Expected reward','File size','Token count','Accuracy only'],answerIndex:0,explanation:'Actions are chosen for the highest expected long-term reward.'}]}]},{id:'sk3',tier:'intermediate',title:'Data Science Harbor',subtitle:'From raw data to decisions',emoji:'\ud83d\udea2',lessons:[{id:'sk3l1',title:'The DS Method',emoji:'\ud83d\udd0d',xp:90,cards:[{emoji:'\u2753',title:'Question first',body:'Great data science starts with a decision to inform, not data to explore. "Should we launch in Brazil?" beats "let\'s look at the data". Define the metric that would change the decision.'},{emoji:'\ud83e\uddea',title:'A/B testing',body:'Split users randomly, show variants, compare metrics. Watch for: sample size (power), peeking early (false positives), and novelty effects. The backbone of product decisions at every tech company.'},{emoji:'\ud83d\udcd6',title:'Storytelling with data',body:'Analysis nobody understands changes nothing. Lead with the recommendation, show the one chart that proves it, keep the details in the appendix. Influence is the final skill of data science.'}],quiz:[{question:'A/B test users must be split\u2026',options:['By preference','Randomly','Alphabetically','By age'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'Randomization removes bias between groups.'},{question:'Peeking at A/B results early causes\u2026',options:['Faster results','Inflated false positives','Better data','Nothing'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'Repeated checks multiply the chance of a fluke "win".'}]},{id:'sk3l2',title:'SQL & Analytics',emoji:'\ud83d\uddc3\ufe0f',xp:90,cards:[{emoji:'\ud83d\uddc3\ufe0f',title:'SQL never dies',body:'SELECT, WHERE, GROUP BY, JOIN \u2014 50-year-old SQL still powers every company\'s analytics. Warehouses (BigQuery, Redshift, Snowflake) run SQL on petabytes. AI engineers who know SQL ship 2x faster.'},{emoji:'\ud83d\udcca',title:'Metrics that matter',body:'DAU/MAU (engagement), retention curves (do users come back?), conversion funnels (where do they drop off?), LTV vs CAC (unit economics). Every AI product lives or dies by these numbers.'},{emoji:'\ud83e\udd16',title:'AI + analytics fusion',body:'Modern stack: LLMs write SQL from questions (text-to-SQL), detect anomalies in metrics, and summarize dashboards in plain English. Semantic layers keep the AI grounded in correct definitions.'}],quiz:[{question:'GROUP BY is used to\u2026',options:['Delete rows','Aggregate rows into groups','Rename tables','Create users'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'It groups rows so you can compute counts, sums, averages per group.'},{question:'Retention measures\u2026',options:['Server uptime','Whether users come back over time','Storage costs','Code quality'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'The most honest signal of product value.'}]}]},{id:'sk4',tier:'advanced',title:'Career Command Center',subtitle:'Turn knowledge into a job',emoji:'\ud83d\udcbc',lessons:[{id:'sk4l1',title:'AI Interviews Decoded',emoji:'\ud83c\udfa4',xp:130,cards:[{emoji:'\ud83c\udfa4',title:'The interview loop',body:'AI/ML roles test: coding (Python/algorithms), ML theory (bias-variance, metrics), ML system design (end-to-end pipelines), and behavioral stories. Each is a separate muscle \u2014 train all four.'},{emoji:'\ud83c\udfd7\ufe0f',title:'System design answers',body:'Framework: clarify requirements \u2192 data \u2192 features \u2192 model \u2192 serving \u2192 monitoring \u2192 iterate. Say tradeoffs OUT LOUD ("batch is cheaper, real-time is fresher"). Interviewers grade thinking, not memorization.'},{emoji:'\ud83d\udcc1',title:'Portfolio > resume',body:'Ship 2-3 real projects: deployed (not just notebooks!), documented READMEs, measurable results. "Built a RAG chatbot serving 200 users, 92% answer accuracy" beats any bullet list of skills.'}],quiz:[{question:'ML system design interviews grade\u2026',options:['Memorized answers','Structured thinking and tradeoffs','Typing speed','GPA'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'The framework and reasoning matter more than the "right" answer.'},{question:'The strongest portfolio project is\u2026',options:['A notebook on your laptop','A deployed app with measurable results','A certificate list','A long resume'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'Deployed + documented + measured = credible.'}]},{id:'sk4l2',title:'Cert Strategy & Beyond',emoji:'\ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f',xp:140,cards:[{emoji:'\ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f',title:'The cert roadmap',body:'Beginner: Azure AI-901 or AWS AI Practitioner. Engineer: AWS ML Engineer Associate or Google Professional ML Engineer. Advanced: AWS GenAI Developer Professional, Microsoft AI-500, or NVIDIA GenAI, Agentic AI, and Infrastructure certifications. Pair every cert with a working project.'},{emoji:'\u23f1\ufe0f',title:'Exam tactics',body:'Eliminate obviously wrong answers first. Flag & skip long scenarios, return later. Watch for keywords: "least operational overhead" = managed service, "cost-effective" = spot/batch, "real-time" = streaming/endpoints. Practice exams > rereading notes.'},{emoji:'\ud83d\ude80',title:'Keep compounding',body:'AI changes monthly \u2014 your learning system matters more than any snapshot of knowledge. Daily streaks here, weekly paper/blog skims, monthly shipped mini-projects. You\'re not studying AI; you\'re living it now. \ud83d\udcaa'}],quiz:[{question:'Which credential is designed as a fundamentals-level starting point?',options:['AWS GenAI Developer Professional','Azure AI-901','NVIDIA Professional AI Infrastructure','None'],answerIndex:1,explanation:'AI-901 is a fundamentals-level on-ramp before engineer and professional credentials.'},{question:'"Least operational overhead" in exams signals\u2026',options:['A managed service answer','Building from scratch','More servers','Manual work'],answerIndex:0,explanation:'Managed/serverless options minimize ops burden.'}]}]}]},282,[]);
__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"lessonGames",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return n}});var t=r(d[0]);const n=Object.assign({w1l1:{kind:'sort',prompt:'Which of these use AI? Sort them!',bins:['\ud83e\udd16 Uses AI','\ud83d\udd27 No AI'],items:[{text:'Face unlock',bin:0},{text:'Netflix suggestions',bin:0},{text:'A mechanical clock',bin:1},{text:'Spam filter',bin:0},{text:'A light switch',bin:1},{text:'Voice assistant',bin:0}]},w1l2:{kind:'order',prompt:'Stack the Russian dolls: biggest concept first!',steps:['Artificial Intelligence','Machine Learning','Deep Learning','Transformers']},w1l3:{kind:'match',prompt:'Match each scenario to its learning type!',pairs:[{left:'Labeled cat/dog photos',right:'Supervised'},{left:'Grouping customers, no labels',right:'Unsupervised'},{left:'Learning chess by rewards',right:'Reinforcement'}]},w2l1:{kind:'sort',prompt:'Features or Label? (predicting house price)',bins:['\ud83d\udcd0 Feature','\ud83c\udfaf Label'],items:[{text:'House size',bin:0},{text:'Location',bin:0},{text:'Sale price',bin:1},{text:'Number of rooms',bin:0},{text:'Year built',bin:0}]},w2l2:{kind:'sort',prompt:'Good data practice or data disaster?',bins:['\u2705 Good practice','\ud83d\udca5 Disaster'],items:[{text:'Clean missing values',bin:0},{text:'Train on one group only',bin:1},{text:'Hold out a test set',bin:0},{text:'Memorize training data',bin:1},{text:'Check for bias',bin:0}]},wb3l1:{kind:'order',prompt:'Put AI history in order!',steps:['Turing Test proposed','Dartmouth coins "AI"','AI winters','Deep learning revolution']},wb3l2:{kind:'order',prompt:'Order the deep learning breakthroughs!',steps:['AlexNet wins ImageNet','AlphaGo beats Go champion','Transformers invented','ChatGPT hits 100M users']},wb4l1:{kind:'match',prompt:'Match the app to its AI engine!',pairs:[{left:'Netflix',right:'Recommender system'},{left:'Similar users liked X',right:'Collaborative filtering'},{left:'Trapped in similar content',right:'Filter bubble'}]},wb4l2:{kind:'order',prompt:'Order the voice assistant pipeline!',steps:['Hear audio (speech-to-text)','Understand intent (NLP)','Decide the answer','Speak reply (text-to-speech)']},wb4l3:{kind:'sort',prompt:'AI fact or AI myth?',bins:['\u2705 Fact','\u274c Myth'],items:[{text:'Today\'s AI is narrow',bin:0},{text:'Chatbots are conscious',bin:1},{text:'AI finds patterns in data',bin:0},{text:'AGI already exists',bin:1},{text:'Humans + AI beat either alone',bin:0}]},w3l1:{kind:'order',prompt:'Build the neural network, layer by layer!',steps:['Input layer (data)','Hidden layer 1 (edges)','Hidden layer 2 (shapes)','Output layer (answer)']},w3l2:{kind:'train',prompt:'Train your first neural network!'},w3l3:{kind:'order',prompt:'How does a CNN see? Order the detection!',steps:['Pixels','Edges & textures','Shapes & parts','Whole objects']},w4l1:{kind:'order',prompt:'Order the NLP pipeline!',steps:['Raw text','Split into tokens','Convert to embeddings','Model processes vectors']},w4l2:{kind:'match',prompt:'Match the LLM concept!',pairs:[{left:'Attention',right:'Weighs which words matter'},{left:'Pretraining',right:'Learn general language'},{left:'RLHF',right:'Align with human feedback'}]},wi3l1:{kind:'sort',prompt:'Regression or Classification?',bins:['\ud83d\udcc8 Regression','\ud83c\udff7\ufe0f Classification'],items:[{text:'Predict house price',bin:0},{text:'Spam or not spam',bin:1},{text:'Tomorrow\'s temperature',bin:0},{text:'Cat vs dog photo',bin:1},{text:'Fraud yes/no',bin:1}]},wi3l2:{kind:'match',prompt:'Match the tree algorithm!',pairs:[{left:'One readable flowchart',right:'Decision tree'},{left:'Many trees voting',right:'Random forest'},{left:'Trees fixing mistakes',right:'Gradient boosting'}]},wi3l3:{kind:'match',prompt:'Match the algorithm to its move!',pairs:[{left:'K-means',right:'Move centers to average'},{left:'KNN',right:'Copy nearest neighbors\' vote'},{left:'Feature scaling',right:'Make distances fair'}]},wi3l4:{kind:'sort',prompt:'Optimize precision or recall?',bins:['\ud83c\udfaf Precision','\ud83d\udd78\ufe0f Recall'],items:[{text:'Spam filter (don\'t block real mail)',bin:0},{text:'Cancer screening (miss nothing)',bin:1},{text:'Arrest warrants (no false accusations)',bin:0},{text:'Airport security (catch every threat)',bin:1}]},wi4l1:{kind:'order',prompt:'Evolution of sequence models \u2014 order them!',steps:['Plain RNN','LSTM with gates','Attention added','Full Transformer']},wi4l2:{kind:'sort',prompt:'Trend, seasonality, or noise?',bins:['\ud83d\uddd3\ufe0f Seasonality','\ud83d\udcc8 Trend'],items:[{text:'Ice cream spikes each summer',bin:0},{text:'Sales growing every year',bin:1},{text:'Traffic dips on weekends',bin:0},{text:'User base steadily rising',bin:1}]},w5l1:{kind:'order',prompt:'How does a diffusion model create an image?',steps:['Start from pure noise','Denoise step by step','Guide with the prompt','Coherent image appears']},w5l2:{kind:'order',prompt:'Build the RAG pipeline!',steps:['User asks a question','Embed the query','Vector search finds documents','LLM answers with context']},wa3l1:{kind:'order',prompt:'Cheapest to most expensive \u2014 order the LLM options!',steps:['Prompt engineering','RAG','Fine-tuning (LoRA)','Train from scratch']},wa3l2:{kind:'match',prompt:'Match the multimodal concept!',pairs:[{left:'CLIP',right:'Shared image-text space'},{left:'Multimodal model',right:'Text + image + audio'},{left:'Embodied AI',right:'Models controlling robots'}]},wa3l3:{kind:'sort',prompt:'Safety technique or safety risk?',bins:['\ud83d\udee1\ufe0f Technique','\ud83d\udea8 Risk'],items:[{text:'RLHF',bin:0},{text:'Prompt injection',bin:1},{text:'Content guardrails',bin:0},{text:'Deepfakes',bin:1},{text:'Human-in-the-loop',bin:0}]},w6l1:{kind:'match',prompt:'Match the cloud to its ML platform!',pairs:[{left:'AWS',right:'SageMaker'},{left:'Azure',right:'Azure ML'},{left:'Google Cloud',right:'Vertex AI'}]},w6l2:{kind:'order',prompt:'Build the MLOps loop!',steps:['Version data & models','Automate training pipeline','Deploy to production','Monitor drift \u2192 retrain']},wa4l1:{kind:'match',prompt:'AWS service showdown \u2014 match them!',pairs:[{left:'Scanned invoices',right:'Textract'},{left:'Foundation models',right:'Bedrock'},{left:'Image recognition',right:'Rekognition'},{left:'Text-to-speech',right:'Polly'}]},wa4l2:{kind:'match',prompt:'Azure service showdown \u2014 match them!',pairs:[{left:'GPT models',right:'Azure OpenAI'},{left:'Vector search for RAG',right:'AI Search'},{left:'Document extraction',right:'Document Intelligence'},{left:'No-code ML concepts',right:'AI-901 exam'}]},wa4l3:{kind:'match',prompt:'GCP service showdown \u2014 match them!',pairs:[{left:'SQL-based ML',right:'BigQuery ML'},{left:'Unified ML platform',right:'Vertex AI'},{left:'Real-time predictions',right:'Online endpoint'},{left:'Bulk offline scoring',right:'Batch prediction'}]},tg1l1:{kind:'match',prompt:'Match the maker to the model!',pairs:[{left:'Anthropic',right:'Claude'},{left:'Google',right:'Gemini'},{left:'OpenAI',right:'GPT'},{left:'Meta (open-source)',right:'Llama'}]},tg1l2:{kind:'sort',prompt:'Cost saver or cost burner?',bins:['\ud83d\udcb0 Saves cost','\ud83d\udd25 Burns cost'],items:[{text:'Smaller model for easy tasks',bin:0},{text:'Max output length always',bin:1},{text:'Prompt caching',bin:0},{text:'Biggest model for everything',bin:1},{text:'Short focused prompts',bin:0}]},tg1l3:{kind:'order',prompt:'Build the perfect prompt, top to bottom!',steps:['Role: "You are an expert\u2026"','Context: background info','Task: clear instruction','Format: how to answer','Examples (few-shot)']},tg1l4:{kind:'match',prompt:'Match the media to the model type!',pairs:[{left:'Images from noise',right:'Diffusion model'},{left:'Cloned narration',right:'Text-to-speech'},{left:'Text clips to video',right:'Video model'}]},tg2l1:{kind:'match',prompt:'Match the cloud to its GenAI platform!',pairs:[{left:'AWS',right:'Bedrock'},{left:'Azure',right:'AI Foundry / OpenAI'},{left:'Google',right:'Vertex AI'}]},tg2l2:{kind:'order',prompt:'Order the semantic search flow!',steps:['Embed all documents','Store vectors in a DB','Embed the user query','Find nearest vectors']},tg2l3:{kind:'order',prompt:'Build production RAG, step by step!',steps:['Chunk the documents','Hybrid search (keyword + vector)','Rerank the results','Generate grounded answer','Evaluate faithfulness']},tg2l4:{kind:'sort',prompt:'Attack or defense?',bins:['\ud83d\udee1\ufe0f Defense','\u2694\ufe0f Attack'],items:[{text:'Prompt injection',bin:1},{text:'Input/output filters',bin:0},{text:'PII masking',bin:0},{text:'Jailbreak attempt',bin:1},{text:'Least-privilege tools',bin:0}]},tg3l1:{kind:'order',prompt:'Climb the customization ladder \u2014 cheapest first!',steps:['Prompting','Few-shot examples','RAG','LoRA fine-tuning','Full fine-tuning','Train from scratch']},tg3l2:{kind:'match',prompt:'Match the inference concept!',pairs:[{left:'Stores attention states',right:'KV cache'},{left:'Draft + verify tokens',right:'Speculative decoding'},{left:'Many requests, one GPU',right:'Continuous batching'},{left:'NVIDIA serving server',right:'Triton'}]},tg3l3:{kind:'sort',prompt:'Good LLMOps or shipping blind?',bins:['\u2705 Good LLMOps','\ud83d\ude48 Shipping blind'],items:[{text:'Custom evals on your data',bin:0},{text:'Trusting benchmark scores only',bin:1},{text:'Prompt versioning',bin:0},{text:'No cost dashboard',bin:1},{text:'Canary deployments',bin:0}]},tm1l1:{kind:'order',prompt:'Order the ML workflow!',steps:['Define the problem','Collect & prepare data','Train the model','Evaluate','Deploy & monitor']},tm1l2:{kind:'match',prompt:'Match the math to its ML job!',pairs:[{left:'Derivative',right:'Which way is downhill'},{left:'Matrix multiply',right:'A network layer'},{left:'Softmax',right:'Scores \u2192 probabilities'}]},tm1l3:{kind:'sort',prompt:'Overfitting fix or overfitting cause?',bins:['\ud83d\udc8a Fix','\ud83e\udda0 Cause'],items:[{text:'Dropout',bin:0},{text:'Model too complex for tiny data',bin:1},{text:'Early stopping',bin:0},{text:'Training too long',bin:1},{text:'L2 regularization',bin:0}]},tm2l1:{kind:'sort',prompt:'Legit feature or data leakage?',bins:['\u2705 Legit feature','\ud83d\udca7 Leakage'],items:[{text:'Customer age',bin:0},{text:'"Refund issued" to predict fraud',bin:1},{text:'Days since last purchase',bin:0},{text:'Tomorrow\'s price in training',bin:1}]},tm2l2:{kind:'match',prompt:'Match the scale-training concept!',pairs:[{left:'Same model, sharded data',right:'Data parallelism'},{left:'Model split across GPUs',right:'Model parallelism'},{left:'Smart hyperparameter search',right:'Bayesian optimization'},{left:'Cheap interruptible GPUs',right:'Spot instances'}]},tm2l3:{kind:'match',prompt:'Match the workload to the deployment!',pairs:[{left:'Chat app, low latency',right:'Real-time endpoint'},{left:'10M rows nightly',right:'Batch transform'},{left:'Spiky rare traffic',right:'Serverless inference'},{left:'Test without user risk',right:'Shadow deployment'}]},tm3l1:{kind:'order',prompt:'Order the automated retraining loop!',steps:['Monitor detects drift','Pipeline retrains model','Evaluate vs champion','Deploy the winner']},tm3l2:{kind:'match',prompt:'Match the responsible-AI tool!',pairs:[{left:'Per-feature explanations',right:'SHAP'},{left:'AWS bias detection',right:'SageMaker Clarify'},{left:'Documented intended use',right:'Model card'}]},tm3l3:{kind:'order',prompt:'Ace the ML system design interview!',steps:['Clarify requirements','Map data sources','Design features & model','Plan serving & latency','Add monitoring & feedback']},ta1l1:{kind:'order',prompt:'Run the agent loop!',steps:['Think about the goal','Act: call a tool','Observe the result','Repeat until done']},ta1l2:{kind:'sort',prompt:'Good tool description or bad?',bins:['\u2705 Good','\u274c Bad'],items:[{text:'"Gets weather by city name"',bin:0},{text:'"Does stuff"',bin:1},{text:'"Searches orders by customer ID"',bin:0},{text:'